    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="VI Atr. Inscr.">[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="VI Atr. Inscr." corresp="#wit-k"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.oe.star2"/>Be<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.oe.1"/> witena gerædnessan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">Be witena gerædnessan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><hi rend="italic">Be witena gerædnessan</hi>:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.de.1"/>Von Beschlüssen der Witan.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.de.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of the decisions of the witan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">Concerning the ordinances of the councillors.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><hi rend="italic">Concerning the decrees of the councilors</hi>:</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="246"><ref target="clause:VAtr_Inscr">V Atr Inscr.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. V[?] Ins[cr.]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="340"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_6">VIII Atr 6–15</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann's base text for 1–15.1 is K (Cotton Claudius A III f. 31v, mid-11th c., after the Latin paraphrase); D (CCCC 201) begins only at 16. ‘K.’ (capitul) stands before each chapter in K. Dated 16 May 1008–13 May 1011. Perhaps VI Atr derives from the same law as V Atr (Liebermann).; AY: added from Rabin p. 160, October 2026 (Rabin’s note to the text)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">Manuscripts: K = London, Cotton MS Claudius A.iii, fols. 35v–37r.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">246</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vielleicht entfloss VI Atr. nur demselben Gesetz wie V Atr.; zu letzterem näher als zu VI Atr. steht, was X Atr. Prol.</hi> 3 <hi rend="italic">als Gesetz</hi> æt Eanham, <hi rend="italic">wo doch VI Atr.</hi> (<hi rend="italic">laut der Paraphrase</hi>) <hi rend="italic">erging, citiert; vgl. o. S.</hi> 236, <hi rend="italic">Sp.</hi> 1**.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps VI Atr. derived only from the same law as V Atr.; what X Atr. Prol. 3 cites as the law æt Eanham, where VI Atr. (according to the Paraphrase) was after all issued, stands closer to the latter than to VI Atr.; cf. above p. 236, col. 1**.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">246</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Be w. g. <hi rend="italic">roth</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Be w. g. in red</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">174</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. Einl. 12ff.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> Introduction 12ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">174</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. Einl. 12ff.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> Introduction 12ff.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.lnote.de.a" n="a" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">174</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">[Die Buchstabennoten beziehen sich auf die Lateinische Paraphrase.] <hi rend="italic">synodalis</hi> hier und 40, 2 nicht ‘geistlich-synodal’, sondern ‘reichstäglich’; <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. Einl. 15. 19</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">[The letter notes refer to the Latin paraphrase.] <hi rend="italic">synodalis</hi> here and in 40, 2 means not ‘ecclesiastical-synodal’ but ‘of the national assembly’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Introduction 15. 19</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.robnote.n.0" n="0" source="#robertson" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">§ 3 and § 4. Cf. V, 9, 1 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.robnote.n.0-2" n="0" source="#robertson" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. V, 19 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.robnote.n.0-3" n="0" source="#robertson" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. V, 21 f.; Wulfstan, p. 271.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VIAtr_Inscr.robnote.n.0-4" n="0" source="#robertson" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. V, 22 f.; I Cn. 19.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
